#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Capture the root window of a virtual display inside the container.
#
#   lab-shot OUT.png DISPLAY SECONDS [COMMAND...]
#
# With COMMAND: start Xvfb on DISPLAY, run COMMAND on it with software GL,
# wait SECONDS, capture, then stop both. With no COMMAND: capture DISPLAY as
# it is, start nothing, stop nothing, so a long-running editor survives.
#
# This file is bash, not Python, deliberately. It is five execs and one pipe
# with no logic of its own, which Python could only wrap in subprocess calls,
# and it must run in every profile's image without requiring python3 there.
# "$@" keeps the caller's argument list intact, so no shell string is ever
# built from it.
#
# Prints one ImageMagick identify line. A caller judges a blank frame from
# stddev and colors without opening the image.

